apps/.env
docs/superpowers/
demo/1_ai-gateway/.env
demo/1_ai-gateway/mock-llm/mock-llm

# `go build ./<dir>/` writes the binary into the CURRENT directory, named after
# the target dir. Building any lab from the repo root therefore drops a
# 80+ MB Mach-O/ELF executable at the root, named "labs" — which is a directory
# in this tree. Never commit it.
/labs

# Local scratch checkouts (e.g. a reference clone of adk-go). Never published.
tmp/
.tmp*
.pi-go/tasks/

# Same story for a single lab: `go build ./week2/<day>/labs3` from the root
# leaves an 80+ MB binary named labs3 at the root, and `cd labs3 && go build .`
# leaves it inside the lab. Paths are relative to this file — no leading "./" —
# and a bare "labs3" would ignore the lab directory itself, so both lines name
# the binary, not the directory.
/labs3
/labs4
week2/*/labs3/labs3
week2/*/labs4/labs4

# The same trap once more, for the demo tree: `go build ./demo/6_adk_telegram_bot`
# from the root drops a 73 MB Mach-O named after the package. Leading slash on
# the first line, so it matches the file at the root and not the directory that
# holds the demo. The second line is the in-place build.
/6_adk_telegram_bot
demo/6_adk_telegram_bot/6_adk_telegram_bot

# And once more for the AG-UI bridge, whose package dir is `demo/agui_web` but
# whose binary is named `agui_web` — `go build ./...` from the root drops a
# 10 MB Mach-O at the root under that name.
/agui_web
demo/agui_web/agui_web

# macOS/VS Code droppings.
.DS_Store

# Week 4 Day 8: Temporal dev server, session store and counters (local state)
.data/
